  'Introduction to ScratchJr': {summary:'ScratchJr is a visual programming environment for young learners. It lets children create stories and simple games by connecting coding blocks.',points:['ScratchJr uses visual blocks instead of requiring typed code.','Projects can include characters and a stage.','Connected blocks tell a character what actions to perform.'],activity:'Open ScratchJr and identify the stage, character and block palette.',illustrations:[['🐱','Character','The object being programmed.'],['🧩','Blocks','Visual instructions.'],['🎬','Stage','Where the project appears.']]},
  'ScratchJr Window and Characters': {summary:'A ScratchJr project uses a stage, characters and coding blocks. Characters can be selected and arranged to create a scene.',points:['The stage displays the project.','Characters are the objects that perform actions.','A project can use more than one character.','Backgrounds help create the scene.'],activity:'Create a new project, choose a character and select a background.',illustrations:[['🎭','Character','Appears on the stage.'],['🌄','Background','Sets the scene.'],['🖥️','Stage','Displays the project.']]},
